s","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-04T10:16:20Z","updated_at":"2025-01-04T10:22:42Z","body":"I have added `string.extend`. The reason is that `String::concat` can trivially be implemented by using `string.extend`, and `string.extend` can be used in even more functions where previously repeated `+=` might have been used.\r\nThis also allowed for an easy add of a `String::concat` specialization for a first-argument rvalue ref `String` that can just be extended in-place, avoiding an unnecessary copy. This optimizes a case where string concatenation via `+` might have previously been faster than `String::concat`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2571137222/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2723303839","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99929#issuecomment-2723303839","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99929","id":2723303839,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iUlGf","user":{"login":"YYF233333","id":67693830,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NjkzODMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67693830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github